{"id": "kufic-course-stride", "verdict": "rewrite", "score": 3, "styleFit": 2, "literal": false, "problems": ["Reads as a code editor minimap or syntax-highlighted lines, not a square Kufic grid rhythm", "Stroke lengths vary freely, so the strict 1 to 1 stroke and gap beat on a square module never shows", "Teal and orange accents appear on many rows, so the brick accent is no longer rare or focal", "Grey, white, teal and orange together make the band busy and clash with the calm surface"], "fix": "Snap every stroke and gap to exactly one square module so the band reads as a woven 1 to 1 grid, with strokes in ink at two tone steps only. Drop teal from the strokes and allow at most one orange module on screen at a time. Keep the edge-gathered layout and the one-module stepped slide, and fade the band toward the open side so it reads as Kufic grid grammar rather than lines of code."}
