```json
{"id": "kintsugi-gold-seam-glint", "verdict": "rewrite", "score": 3, "styleFit": 3, "literal": true, "problems": ["Reads as a picture of a cracked, gold-mended bowl: jagged crack path, branch and embossed shadow mime the repair itself", "The seam runs through the vertical middle of the frame, cutting across where a headline or control would sit", "The branch has a muddy, smeared shadow that looks unfinished next to the clean main line", "The glint is pleasant but generic; it adds little beyond a shimmer pass"], "fix": "Abstract the kintsugi idea into a rule: one calm hairline of gold that marks where something was rejoined, drawn as a smooth, barely wavering line along a lower or edge third with no crack branch or emboss. Keep the faint speckle as a second voice and let the glint settle once to mark the recovered state, aiming for a quiet minimal-mono-light card surface."}
