```json
{"id": "najdi-door-swing-open", "verdict": "rewrite", "score": 2, "styleFit": 2, "literal": true, "problems": ["A left-hinged 3D rotateY swing mimes the door itself; it is the stock door-open transition with a craft name attached.", "Nothing of Najdi door grammar survives: no framed panel structure, no triangle rhythm, no earth-wall weight.", "The hinge sits on the left edge, so the swing reads left to right and ignores the right-to-left mirroring the gulf-arabic-first tag requires.", "Fading to opacity 0 while past 90 degrees hides the end state, so the gesture reads as a generic flip-out rather than a settled reveal."], "fix": "Drop the literal hinge rotation and borrow the door's construction instead: reveal the screen through its framed panel, with an inset frame that steps open in a staggered row of triangular bands (around 40 ms apart, cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.7, 0.2, 1), about 360 ms in total) and a flat, heavy, matte settle. Mirror the origin and the stagger direction for RTL so the reveal reads right to left, and keep the plain fade for reduced motion."}
```

```json
{"id": "screen-wall-rows-into-shade", "verdict": "rewrite", "score": 3, "styleFit": 3, "literal": false, "problems": ["The flare is hidden. Brightness peaks at opacity 0 and falls as the row fades in, so the sun to shade idea never reads.", "On a light mono UI, brightness(1.25) on white or pale rows clips to white and does nothing.", "Without the flare this is a stock 16px staggered slide-in with no borrowed rhythm from the concrete screen."], "fix": "Make the shade the move. Bring opacity to 1 within the first 30% so the row is seen lit, then settle it into its resting tone with a short filter step (contrast or a slight darken, not brightness above 1), using a firm decelerating curve. Borrow the screen's modular grid for the stagger by advancing rows in even fixed beats, so it reads as calm and crisp for minimal-mono-light."}
```

```json
{"id": "cordel-string-sway-in", "verdict": "rewrite", "score": 3, "styleFit": 3, "literal": false, "problems": ["A -5deg start rotation on full-width list rows throws the row ends far off line. Mid-run, rows tilt and crowd each other, so the list reads wobbly rather than hung.", "Three swing reversals (2.5, -1, 0) packed into 360 ms is busy for a list. Repeated on every row it starts to feel like a gimmick, not a settle.", "The pivot at 50% 0% swings each row around its top centre like a pendulum on a nail. Cordel sheets hang from a string pegged at the corners, so the pivot does not match the source either."], "fix": "Keep the damped hang-and-settle, but cap rotation near 1.5deg for list rows (keep about 3deg only for single cards). Use one small overshoot and one settle on a custom spring-like curve, around 300 ms with a 40 to 50 ms stagger. Lead with the short drop rather than the twist, so the motion borrows the light, slightly loose feel of paper on a line without wagging every row."}
```

```json
{"id": "alula-strata-settle", "verdict": "rewrite", "score": 3, "styleFit": 2, "literal": false, "problems": ["Bands are soft blurred smudges in a muddy grey-brown, so they read as a generic wavy-line shader rather than warm sandstone or a printed hand", "Bands spread evenly down the whole frame, leaving no clear calm zone for text despite the stated calm top", "The one hard sun angle from the card is missing: bands have no lit top edge or tonal step, so there is no depth", "The hairline layers inside the bands are barely visible, so texture does not register as a second voice"], "fix": "Keep the settle and the one rust divider, but give each band a crisp, slightly irregular printed edge with a lit top lip and a shadowed underside from one fixed sun angle. Use warm tones stepped from #d9a88a, make the inner hairlines and grain clearly visible, and keep the top 40% pale and empty so it reads as illustrative-handmade strata behind real type."}
```

