{"id": "rawasheen-bay-stack", "verdict": "rewrite", "score": 2, "styleFit": 2, "literal": true, "problems": ["Draws the roshan itself: framed wooden windows with two door panels below the lattice and a drop shadow, a picture of the object.", "The diagonal light sweep across each lattice reads as a stock gloss highlight, not filtered light.", "A column of window icons drifting up a wall reads as scrolling wallpaper, the cheap 'pattern as wallpaper' Gulf look.", "The coral stone coursing is so faint it adds no second voice, and the drop shadow fights the flat, made feel."], "fix": "Keep the lens grammar and drop the windows. Use tall vertical bands of fine slat lattice at the even 1:2 bay to wall rhythm, with no frames, door panels or shadows, on a calm sand or near-black surface with faint coursed hairlines. Light a few cells at a time with a slow halftone-like falloff, as sun filtered through mashrabiya, and aim for restrained gulf-arabic-first texture that leaves the plain wall as clear space for text."}
```

