```json
{"id": "kintsugi-seam-mend", "verdict": "rewrite", "score": 3, "styleFit": 3, "literal": false, "problems": ["The kintsugi idea is the marked seam, but the recipe only does a generic settle from a crooked offset. Nothing marks where the repair happened.", "The reduced-motion state promises a gold seam that the keyframes never produce, so the two states disagree.", "A saturate and brightness lift reads as almost nothing on a quiet mono-light field, so the warming is lost.", "Rotating a form field by 1.2 degrees can look wobbly next to aligned inputs."], "fix": "Keep the short settle (about 320 to 380ms on the same expo-out curve) but drop the rotation to a 2px translate only. Carry the mend in one hairline accent instead: an inset box-shadow or border on one edge that brightens once to the accent and then rests as a thin seam, matching the reduced-motion end state, for a calm minimal-mono-light feel."}
